    "created_at": "2019-08-20T10:55:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-08-20T10:55:31Z",
    "body": "Wondering if `jobs -d` could be a solution. This will display the specific pwd for each job. The output should thus always have 2 lines per job, and there is no unexpected final line any more. The output is the same whether you pipe to `cat` or not.\r\n\r\nNote that `-d` is not available on all shells, so may have to be added only for zsh.\r\n\r\n```\r\nin ~/Downloads/yt \r\n✦2  jobs -d | cat\r\n[1]  - suspended  sleep 5\r\n(pwd : ~/test/a)\r\n[2]  + suspended  sleep 10\r\n(pwd : ~/test)\r\n```\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
