    "created_at": "2019-08-28T05:48:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-08-28T05:48:35Z",
    "body": "Possible solution without using math: https://www.zsh.org/mla/users/2001/msg00706.html\r\n\r\nUse zmodule zsh/parameter, we can do\r\n\r\n```\r\n$#jobstates\r\n```\r\n\r\nto get the number of jobs.\r\n\r\nThe linked forum post claims that this has been a ZSH module since 3.1.9, which came out in August 2000 (!!), so we should be just fine loading this.\r\n\r\nIn addition, ZSH 5.7.1 (current) seems to autoload this module when needed, e.g. if you run `zmodload -L`, then run `echo $#jobstates` and run `zmodload -L` again, you'll see that this module has been automatically loaded for you.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
